('5de63d81-aaa9-588c-a401-d0a1ef31c185','fcba1b6c-b06e-574e-a9ba-447f1d49a02a',6,'job/work','شغل/کار','spoken & written','a particular job, especially one needing special skill with your hands','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'یک شغل خاص، به خصوص شغلی که نیاز به مهارت خاصی با دستان شما دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['international/foreign trade International trade is essential for long-term economic growth.','global/world trade We want the poorer nations to benefit from increased global trade.','the arms/timber/book etc trade Britain is heavily involved in the arms trade.','the drugs/slave trade the country’s thriving drugs trade','the tourist trade The wildlife and scenery have helped to make the tourist trade Alaska''s second industry','the retail trade (= businesses which sell goods in shops to customers ) Advertising encourages the retail trade to stock and display the product.','the wholesale trade (= businesses which sell goods in large quantities at low prices to other businesses, rather than to the general public ) In the domestic market, the wholesale trade and retail trade developed rapidly.','trade barriers ( also barriers to trade formal ) (= things that make trade between two countries more difficult or expensive, such as taxes ) The removal of trade barriers will help our trading partnership.','a trade agreement On April 3 a new trade agreement between Romania and the USA was signed.','a trade embargo (= an official order to stop trade with another country ) Delegates urged the US government to lift its trade embargo against Vietnam.','trade talks/negotiations A further round of trade talks begins this week in Geneva.','a trade deficit (= the amount by which the total goods one country sells to others is less than the amount it buys from them ) The foreign trade deficit widened by 42% compared with the previous year.','a trade surplus (= the amount by which the total goods one country sells to others is more than the amount it buys from them ) Scotch whisky is a major contributor to the UK trade balance, with a large trade surplus.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Brian insisted that his sons learn a trade .","translation":"برایان اصرار داشت که پسرانش حرفه ای بیاموزند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001736537.mp3"},{"sentence":"My grandfather was a plumber by trade (= that was his job ) .","translation":"پدربزرگ من لوله کش بود (= شغلش همین بود).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001736541.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('638d63f8-364d-5bfb-95f2-6d0e8a87958b','beec3c15-5ae0-5bf5-abde-4d72043b13d9',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to buy and sell goods, services etc as your job or business','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'تجارت کردن؛ سوداگری کردن (بازار)؛ معاوضه کردن (با)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"India began trading with Europe in the 15th and 16th centuries.","translation":"هند تجارت با اروپا را در قرن 15 و 16 آغاز کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000552118.mp3"},{"sentence":"The company trades in silk, tea, and other items.","translation":"این شرکت ابریشم، چای و اقلام دیگر را تجارت می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000552121.mp3"},{"sentence":"They had to travel into town to trade the produce from their farm.","translation":"آنها مجبور بودند برای تجارت محصولات مزرعه خود به شهر سفر کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000552124.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
