('ca526f20-43ae-5f39-b718-2d9ee2da8469','15997068-2eca-5b8f-b624-048b21d64e14',1,null,null,'spoken & written','things that you throw away, such as empty bottles , used papers, food that has gone bad etc',null,null,'زباله، آشغال؛ زباله (دست)؛ زباله (سینی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Will someone take out the trash (= take it outside the house ) ?","translation":"آیا کسی سطل زباله را بیرون می آورد (= آن را به بیرون از خانه می برد)؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001613820.mp3"},{"sentence":"Just put it in the trash .","translation":"فقط آن را در سطل زباله قرار دهید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001613824.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('4c9df993-30cf-524e-9d51-846644a4d502','15997068-2eca-5b8f-b624-048b21d64e14',2,null,null,'informal','something that is of very poor quality',null,null,'چیزی که کیفیتش خیلی پایینه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"How can you read that trash?","translation":"چگونه می توانید آن زباله ها را بخوانید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000555282.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('2f0803d4-891a-5611-a819-1310b06f1eaa','15997068-2eca-5b8f-b624-048b21d64e14',3,null,null,'informal','someone from a low social class who you do not respect because you think they are lazy or immoral',null,'white trash','فردی از یک طبقه اجتماعی پایین که به او احترام نمی گذارید زیرا فکر می کنید تنبل یا بداخلاق است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('c340b85e-2aae-5e93-b827-16d344841b69','613488bd-1934-5f5e-9cb8-f2c937ab290a',1,null,null,'informal','to destroy something completely, either deliberately or by using it too much',null,null,'نابود کردن چیزی به طور کامل، عمدا یا با استفاده بیش از حد از آن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The place got trashed last time we had a party.","translation":"آخرین باری که مهمانی داشتیم، مکان سطل زباله شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000555297.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('bf0d061d-e290-58ab-9052-f7ec7d915d44','613488bd-1934-5f5e-9cb8-f2c937ab290a',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to criticize someone or something very severely',null,null,'انتقاد شدید از کسی یا چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The researchers are angry that attempts have been made to trash their work.","translation":"محققان از این که تلاش شده کار آنها به زباله ریخته شود، عصبانی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001613837.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('6ffe4f0e-0c2c-5933-9c8e-097d7f95c7d2','1b286b7b-1471-56a2-b0aa-2f5b7f4bde5a',1,'behave towards somebody/something','نسبت به کسی/چیزی رفتار کردن','spoken & written','to behave towards someone or something in a particular way','[ always + adverb/preposition ]',null,'رفتار کردن با؛ برخورد کردن (با)؛ درمان کردن (بیمار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['well The majority of workers are well treated.','badly Why did he treat me so badly?','fairly/unfairly I just want to be treated fairly.','equally All people should be treated equally, whatever their age.','differently Should girls be treated differently from boys in school?','harshly The guards treated the prisoners harshly.','kindly The world had not treated him kindly.','treat somebody with respect/contempt/suspicion etc When you treat the kids with respect, they act responsibly.','treat somebody like dirt informal (= very badly and with no respect ) He treated this wife like dirt.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She treats me like one of the family.","translation":"او با من مثل یکی از اعضای خانواده رفتار می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000556200.mp3"},{"sentence":"Penny doesn’t think her co-workers treat her as an equal.","translation":"پنی فکر نمی کند که همکارانش با او به عنوان یک برابر رفتار می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656221.mp3"},{"sentence":"He treated his automobiles almost as tenderly as he did his wife.","translation":"او تقریباً به همان مهربانی با همسرش با اتومبیل هایش رفتار می کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656222.mp3"},{"sentence":"The prisoners were well treated by their guards.","translation":"نگهبانان با زندانیان رفتار خوبی داشتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000556204.mp3"},{"sentence":"Despite her seniority, Margot was never treated with much respect.","translation":"مارگو علیرغم سن بالایی که داشت، هرگز با احترام زیادی برخورد نکرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000556207.mp3"},{"sentence":"I don’t know why he stays with her – she treats him like dirt.","translation":"نمی‌دانم چرا با او می‌ماند - او با او مانند کثیفی رفتار می‌کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656223.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('6746b422-2fd7-58b5-a59c-8036808b8982','1b286b7b-1471-56a2-b0aa-2f5b7f4bde5a',2,'deal with something','با چیزی برخورد کن','spoken & written','to deal with, regard , or consider something in a particular way','[ always + adverb/preposition ]',null,'برخورد کردن، توجه کردن یا در نظر گرفتن چیزی به روشی خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['well The majority of workers are well treated.','badly Why did he treat me so badly?','fairly/unfairly I just want to be treated fairly.','equally All people should be treated equally, whatever their age.','differently Should girls be treated differently from boys in school?','harshly The guards treated the prisoners harshly.','kindly The world had not treated him kindly.','treat somebody with respect/contempt/suspicion etc When you treat the kids with respect, they act responsibly.','treat somebody like dirt informal (= very badly and with no respect ) He treated this wife like dirt.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Please treat this information as completely confidential.","translation":"لطفاً این اطلاعات را کاملاً محرمانه تلقی کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000556218.mp3"},{"sentence":"She treats everything I say as a joke.","translation":"او با هر چیزی که من می گویم به عنوان یک شوخی برخورد می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000556234.mp3"},{"sentence":"Any complaint about safety standards must be treated very seriously.","translation":"هر گونه شکایت در مورد استانداردهای ایمنی باید بسیار جدی برخورد شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000556221.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('d800f84f-59f2-5bd5-95a6-ed7b44870321','1b286b7b-1471-56a2-b0aa-2f5b7f4bde5a',3,'illness/injury','بیماری / جراحت','spoken & written','to try to cure an illness or injury by using drugs , hospital care , operations etc',null,null,'تلاش برای درمان یک بیماری یا جراحت با استفاده از داروها، مراقبت های بیمارستانی، عملیات و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['well The majority of workers are well treated.','badly Why did he treat me so badly?','fairly/unfairly I just want to be treated fairly.','equally All people should be treated equally, whatever their age.','differently Should girls be treated differently from boys in school?','harshly The guards treated the prisoners harshly.','kindly The world had not treated him kindly.','treat somebody with respect/contempt/suspicion etc When you treat the kids with respect, they act responsibly.','treat somebody like dirt informal (= very badly and with no respect ) He treated this wife like dirt.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"It was difficult to treat patients because of a shortage of medicine.","translation":"درمان بیماران به دلیل کمبود دارو دشوار بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656224.mp3"},{"sentence":"Nowadays, malaria can be treated with drugs.","translation":"امروزه مالاریا را می توان با دارو درمان کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000556226.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('43065ad5-cd44-5327-81dd-34dc81132126','1b286b7b-1471-56a2-b0aa-2f5b7f4bde5a',4,'buy something for somebody','برای کسی چیزی بخر','spoken & written','to buy or do something special for someone that you know they will enjoy',null,null,'برای خرید یا انجام کاری خاص برای کسی که می دانید از آن لذت خواهد برد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['well The majority of workers are well treated.','badly Why did he treat me so badly?','fairly/unfairly I just want to be treated fairly.','equally All people should be treated equally, whatever their age.','differently Should girls be treated differently from boys in school?','harshly The guards treated the prisoners harshly.','kindly The world had not treated him kindly.','treat somebody with respect/contempt/suspicion etc When you treat the kids with respect, they act responsibly.','treat somebody like dirt informal (= very badly and with no respect ) He treated this wife like dirt.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We treated Mom to lunch at the Savoy.","translation":"ناهار را در ساووی از مادر پذیرایی کردیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000556241.mp3"},{"sentence":"I treated myself to a new dress.","translation":"من خودم را با یک لباس جدید پذیرفتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000556245.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('4eb5d36b-92da-5f5f-be2c-01ec48f2b690','1b286b7b-1471-56a2-b0aa-2f5b7f4bde5a',5,'protect/clean','محافظت / تمیز کردن','spoken & written','to put a special substance on something or use a chemical process in order to protect , clean , or preserve it',null,null,'قرار دادن ماده ای خاص بر روی چیزی یا استفاده از فرآیند شیمیایی به منظور محافظت، تمیز کردن یا حفظ آن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['well The majority of workers are well treated.','badly Why did he treat me so badly?','fairly/unfairly I just want to be treated fairly.','equally All people should be treated equally, whatever their age.','differently Should girls be treated differently from boys in school?','harshly The guards treated the prisoners harshly.','kindly The world had not treated him kindly.','treat somebody with respect/contempt/suspicion etc When you treat the kids with respect, they act responsibly.','treat somebody like dirt informal (= very badly and with no respect ) He treated this wife like dirt.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"sewage treated so that it can be used as fertilizer","translation":"فاضلاب تصفیه می شود تا بتوان از آن به عنوان کود استفاده کرد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000556250.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('73a76b16-a3da-5b72-9928-e72f69f5bfce','3ce7ae7e-a155-5932-b6e9-b2c94930116b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','something special that you give someone or do for them because you know they will enjoy it','[ countable ]',null,'پذیرایی، پذیرایی (مهمان)؛ پذیرایی (فرد)؛ پذیرایی (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Steven took his son to a cricket match as a birthday treat.","translation":"استیون پسرش را به عنوان هدیه تولد به مسابقه کریکت برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000557764.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('4ddca028-8abe-5f04-aebf-679fcd75e03d','3ce7ae7e-a155-5932-b6e9-b2c94930116b',2,null,null,'spoken & written','an event that gives you a lot of pleasure and is usually unexpected','[ singular ]',null,'اتفاقی که به شما لذت زیادی می‌دهد و معمولاً غیرمنتظره است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"When we were kids, a trip to the beach was a real treat .","translation":"وقتی بچه بودیم، سفر به ساحل لذت واقعی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656235.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ed54ca6a-f636-59c3-81a6-9960855f8d5e','3ce7ae7e-a155-5932-b6e9-b2c94930116b',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a special food that tastes good, especially one that you do not eat very often','[ countable ]',null,'یک غذای خاص که طعم خوبی دارد، مخصوصاً غذایی که زیاد آن را نمی خورید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The cafe serves an assortment of gourmet treats.","translation":"در این کافه انواع غذاهای لذیذ سرو می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656243.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('f99662cc-9e6c-57f4-969d-ff4f34c7e9e3','3ce7ae7e-a155-5932-b6e9-b2c94930116b',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'my treat','پذیرایی، پذیرایی (مهمان)؛ پذیرایی (فرد)؛ پذیرایی (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('ee71d97e-61c9-5378-8ba1-e8c0bb266d71','3ce7ae7e-a155-5932-b6e9-b2c94930116b',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'go down a treat','پذیرایی، پذیرایی (مهمان)؛ پذیرایی (فرد)؛ پذیرایی (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('7b0253e4-b9cb-543d-8cac-b7d5ff161d94','3ce7ae7e-a155-5932-b6e9-b2c94930116b',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'look/work a treat','پذیرایی، پذیرایی (مهمان)؛ پذیرایی (فرد)؛ پذیرایی (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('67921c72-26ba-53bc-97d6-fcdc5cbbf224','54d7e23f-51f7-540b-893f-90525639b0e8',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a general tendency in the way a situation is changing or developing',null,null,'روند، گرایش؛ روند (بازار)؛ روند (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a recent/new trend He wrote an article attacking many recent trends in education.','the current/latest trend If current trends continue, the amount of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere will double by the year 2030.','a general trend (= one followed by most people or happening in most places ) There was a general trend towards marriage at a younger age.','a growing/increasing/rising trend a growing trend towards globalization in world markets','an alarming/worrying/disturbing trend I have detected a worrying trend of late.','the underlying/long-term trend (= the trend over a long period of time ) The underlying trend is for rich economies to get richer.','a downward/upward trend (= a tendency for something to increase or decrease ) The downward trend in population growth was not seen as a problem.','economic/market trends This forecast is based on current economic trends.','the national trend Crime rates in Manchester bucked the national trend.','the international/world-wide/global trend the global trend towards intensive farming','reverse a trend (= make something start to change back ) He succeeded in reversing the downward trend of the railway’s fortunes.','buck the trend (= do something that is not what is generally happening ) The recession may still be biting, but video games company Nintendo continues to buck the trend.','follow a trend Divorce rates in Scotland are following the general trend.','start a trend The young started a trend toward living in the downtown area.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Lately there has been a trend towards hiring younger, cheaper employees.","translation":"اخیراً گرایشی به سمت استخدام کارمندان جوان تر و ارزان تر وجود داشته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656362.mp3"},{"sentence":"recent trends in education","translation":"روندهای اخیر در آموزش و پرورش","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000558328.mp3"},{"sentence":"The current trend is towards more part-time employment.","translation":"روند فعلی به سمت اشتغال پاره وقت بیشتر است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845808.mp3"},{"sentence":"the general trend towards the centralization of political power","translation":"گرایش عمومی به تمرکز قدرت سیاسی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845812.mp3"},{"sentence":"A disturbing trend is that victims of violence are getting younger.","translation":"یک روند نگران کننده این است که قربانیان خشونت در حال جوان تر شدن هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845816.mp3"},{"sentence":"The growing trend is for single mothers to bring up children by themselves.","translation":"روند رو به رشد این است که مادران مجرد فرزندان خود را بزرگ کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845820.mp3"},{"sentence":"Even so, the underlying trend is positive.","translation":"با این حال، روند اساسی مثبت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845824.mp3"},{"sentence":"national and international economic trends","translation":"روندهای اقتصادی ملی و بین المللی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845828.mp3"},{"sentence":"the downward trend in the price of gold","translation":"روند نزولی قیمت طلا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845831.mp3"},{"sentence":"Successive presidents have tried to reverse this trend , but without success.","translation":"روسای جمهور متوالی تلاش کردند تا این روند را معکوس کنند، اما موفق نشدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845835.mp3"}]'::jsonb,10),
