('4272e0e2-48a9-5149-bd24-b87f509a10ad','e573d04f-30b1-5352-aafb-72105e6990fa',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if a subject is trending on the Internet , a lot of people are searching for it or sending messages about it',null,null,'اگر موضوعی در اینترنت پرطرفدار باشد، افراد زیادی آن را جستجو می کنند یا در مورد آن پیام ارسال می کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('7934fe1c-4336-5b87-921a-c5b26e3a320d','e573d04f-30b1-5352-aafb-72105e6990fa',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if an amount is trending downwards or upwards , it is becoming lower or higher',null,null,'اگر مقداری روند رو به پایین یا صعودی داشته باشد، در حال کاهش یا بالاتر شدن است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Average temperatures are trending upwards.","translation":"میانگین دما روند صعودی دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ld5_upd08_010.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('0057298f-ad3d-56fc-83eb-795f8a632e64','e2371dc6-8f87-591a-96fa-3252e8a0a8a8',1,'court','دادگاه','spoken & written','a legal process in which a judge and often a jury in a court of law examine information to decide whether someone is guilty of a crime','[ countable, uncountable ]','show trial','محاکمه، دادرسی؛ محاکمه (فرد)؛ آزمایش (تاثیر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be on trial (= be being judged in a court of law ) Her son is on trial charged with murder.','stand/face trial (= be judged in a court of law ) Doctors said he was unfit to stand trial.','go on trial Taylor went on trial accused of fraud.','be awaiting/facing trial Its managing director is awaiting trial on corruption charges.','put somebody on trial They should never have been put on trial, let alone convicted.','bring somebody to trial The people who were responsible for this crime must be brought to trial.','be sent for trial ( also be committed for trial British English ) Smith''s lawyer battled to stop him being sent for trial in Britain.','a trial is held We believe the trial will be held sometime next month.','a trial opens (= officially begins ) The trial opened 5 weeks ago.','a trial is adjourned (= it is officially stopped for several days, weeks, or months ) The trial was adjourned until November.','a murder/fraud etc trial She was a witness in a murder trial.','a fair trial He is entitled to a fair trial.','a criminal trial (= for cases involving a crime ) In a criminal trial, guilt has to be proven beyond reasonable doubt.','a civil trial (= for cases dealing with the private affairs of citizens, rather than cases involving a crime ) In civil trials, the jury''s decision need not be unanimous.','a case goes/comes to trial If the case ever went to trial, he would probably lose.','the trial judge The trial judge acquitted the accused on the charge of assault.','the trial lawyer He is regarded as one of the finest trial lawyers in the state.','the trial court The evidence will be fully tested in the trial court.','a trial date No trial date has been set because of procedural delays.','the trial verdict His lawyers have said they will appeal the civil trial verdict.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The trial is due to start next week.","translation":"دادگاه قرار است هفته آینده آغاز شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001637.mp3"},{"sentence":"Brady was on trial for assault.","translation":"برادی به اتهام حمله به دادگاه محاکمه شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000558587.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('bb0bdf00-7c0e-57d1-8a29-c711bcb698d9','e2371dc6-8f87-591a-96fa-3252e8a0a8a8',2,'test','تست کنید','spoken & written','a process of testing to find out whether something works effectively and is safe','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'یک فرآیند آزمایش برای یافتن اینکه آیا چیزی به طور موثر کار می کند و ایمن است یا خیر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be on trial (= be being judged in a court of law ) Her son is on trial charged with murder.','stand/face trial (= be judged in a court of law ) Doctors said he was unfit to stand trial.','go on trial Taylor went on trial accused of fraud.','be awaiting/facing trial Its managing director is awaiting trial on corruption charges.','put somebody on trial They should never have been put on trial, let alone convicted.','bring somebody to trial The people who were responsible for this crime must be brought to trial.','be sent for trial ( also be committed for trial British English ) Smith''s lawyer battled to stop him being sent for trial in Britain.','a trial is held We believe the trial will be held sometime next month.','a trial opens (= officially begins ) The trial opened 5 weeks ago.','a trial is adjourned (= it is officially stopped for several days, weeks, or months ) The trial was adjourned until November.','a murder/fraud etc trial She was a witness in a murder trial.','a fair trial He is entitled to a fair trial.','a criminal trial (= for cases involving a crime ) In a criminal trial, guilt has to be proven beyond reasonable doubt.','a civil trial (= for cases dealing with the private affairs of citizens, rather than cases involving a crime ) In civil trials, the jury''s decision need not be unanimous.','a case goes/comes to trial If the case ever went to trial, he would probably lose.','the trial judge The trial judge acquitted the accused on the charge of assault.','the trial lawyer He is regarded as one of the finest trial lawyers in the state.','the trial court The evidence will be fully tested in the trial court.','a trial date No trial date has been set because of procedural delays.','the trial verdict His lawyers have said they will appeal the civil trial verdict.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a new drug that is undergoing clinical trials","translation":"داروی جدیدی که در حال انجام آزمایشات بالینی است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000558604.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('2738066f-02f6-5b71-94a4-5c28e1a793b7','e2371dc6-8f87-591a-96fa-3252e8a0a8a8',3,'try somebody/something','کسی/چیزی را امتحان کن','spoken & written','a short period during which you use or do something or employ someone to find out whether they are satisfactory for a particular purpose or job','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'دوره کوتاهی که در طی آن از کاری استفاده می‌کنید یا انجام می‌دهید یا شخصی را استخدام می‌کنید تا بفهمید آیا برای یک هدف یا شغل خاص رضایت‌بخش است یا خیر.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be on trial (= be being judged in a court of law ) Her son is on trial charged with murder.','stand/face trial (= be judged in a court of law ) Doctors said he was unfit to stand trial.','go on trial Taylor went on trial accused of fraud.','be awaiting/facing trial Its managing director is awaiting trial on corruption charges.','put somebody on trial They should never have been put on trial, let alone convicted.','bring somebody to trial The people who were responsible for this crime must be brought to trial.','be sent for trial ( also be committed for trial British English ) Smith''s lawyer battled to stop him being sent for trial in Britain.','a trial is held We believe the trial will be held sometime next month.','a trial opens (= officially begins ) The trial opened 5 weeks ago.','a trial is adjourned (= it is officially stopped for several days, weeks, or months ) The trial was adjourned until November.','a murder/fraud etc trial She was a witness in a murder trial.','a fair trial He is entitled to a fair trial.','a criminal trial (= for cases involving a crime ) In a criminal trial, guilt has to be proven beyond reasonable doubt.','a civil trial (= for cases dealing with the private affairs of citizens, rather than cases involving a crime ) In civil trials, the jury''s decision need not be unanimous.','a case goes/comes to trial If the case ever went to trial, he would probably lose.','the trial judge The trial judge acquitted the accused on the charge of assault.','the trial lawyer He is regarded as one of the finest trial lawyers in the state.','the trial court The evidence will be fully tested in the trial court.','a trial date No trial date has been set because of procedural delays.','the trial verdict His lawyers have said they will appeal the civil trial verdict.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"They let me have the computer on trial for thirty days.","translation":"آنها به من اجازه دادند کامپیوتر را به مدت سی روز آزمایشی داشته باشم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000558611.mp3"},{"sentence":"The security system will be reviewed after a three-month trial period .","translation":"سیستم امنیتی پس از یک دوره آزمایشی سه ماهه بررسی خواهد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000558614.mp3"},{"sentence":"Smith was hired on a six-month trial basis .","translation":"اسمیت به صورت آزمایشی شش ماهه استخدام شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001656444.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
