('9955ef33-8db1-529b-b1bc-db3c893d19bc','460d1e5b-c5b3-5345-aa94-f32b63c6bf0b',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'position of trust','اعتماد، اطمینان؛ اعتماد (مالی)؛ اعتماد (حالت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('7dad57df-8430-5fb9-8de4-68f4c7c716b2','460d1e5b-c5b3-5345-aa94-f32b63c6bf0b',6,'companies','شرکت ها','spoken & written','a group of companies that illegally work together to reduce competition and control prices','[ countable ]',null,'گروهی از شرکت ها که به طور غیرقانونی با یکدیگر همکاری می کنند تا رقابت را کاهش دهند و قیمت ها را کنترل کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"anti-trust laws","translation":"قوانین ضد تراست","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000562420.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c628202c-d9ee-5fb5-968d-2b0958d0b37d','9dfaf997-959c-500a-ace8-78801e5a0d18',1,'people','مردم','spoken & written','to believe that someone is honest or will not do anything bad or wrong',null,null,'اعتماد کردن، اطمینان داشتن (به)؛ اعتماد (دارایی)؛ سپردن (به)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I just don’t trust him.","translation":"من فقط به او اعتماد ندارم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000562443.mp3"},{"sentence":"Can they be trusted to look after the house?","translation":"آیا می توان به آنها برای مراقبت از خانه اعتماد کرد؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000562446.mp3"},{"sentence":"I didn’t trust myself not to say something rude, so I just kept quiet.","translation":"من به خودم اعتماد نداشتم که حرف بی ادبی نزنم، بنابراین فقط سکوت کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001600794.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was a good driver and I trusted him implicitly.","translation":"او راننده خوبی بود و من به طور ضمنی به او اعتماد داشتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000562449.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('a9521bd2-6de9-53c1-81c7-1f72b80fce01','9dfaf997-959c-500a-ace8-78801e5a0d18',2,'facts/judgment','حقایق / قضاوت','spoken & written','to be sure that something is correct or right',null,null,'مطمئن شوید که چیزی درست یا درست است',array['believe in','rely on']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Can we trust these statistics?","translation":"آیا می توان به این آمار اعتماد کرد؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000562465.mp3"},{"sentence":"I trust his judgement completely.","translation":"من به قضاوت او کاملاً اعتماد دارم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001600795.mp3"},{"sentence":"Trust your instincts (= do what you feel is the right thing ) !","translation":"به غریزه خود اعتماد کنید (= کاری را که فکر می کنید درست است انجام دهید)!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001600801.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('081d20c5-7ca5-5102-8817-afc41636d12d','9dfaf997-959c-500a-ace8-78801e5a0d18',3,'things','چیزها','spoken & written','to be sure that something will work properly',null,null,'مطمئن شوید که چیزی به درستی کار خواهد کرد',array['rely on']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Not trusting her voice, she shook her head.","translation":"به صدایش اعتماد نکرد، سرش را تکان داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001600810.mp3"},{"sentence":"You can’t trust the trains to run on time.","translation":"نمی توانید به حرکت قطارها به موقع اعتماد کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000562468.mp3"},{"sentence":"He sat down suddenly, as if he didn’t trust his legs to support him.","translation":"او ناگهان نشست، انگار به پاهایش برای حمایت از او اعتماد نداشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001600813.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('afd6f21b-ce26-5b3d-a82d-e1d085c4cccc','9dfaf997-959c-500a-ace8-78801e5a0d18',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'trust you/him/them etc (to do something)!','اعتماد کردن، اطمینان داشتن (به)؛ اعتماد (دارایی)؛ سپردن (به)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('ffa3181a-ffc5-5cad-8710-41d7ecf098b4','9dfaf997-959c-500a-ace8-78801e5a0d18',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'I trust (that)','اعتماد کردن، اطمینان داشتن (به)؛ اعتماد (دارایی)؛ سپردن (به)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f6560cc1-8a7c-56a2-b46b-c1dee49ab811','1af0b85a-4dc9-57f2-860a-a2e4c48b66ed',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the truth','حقیقت، راستی؛ حقیقت (طی)؛ حقیقت (زندگی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['tell the truth It’s better to tell the truth.','speak the truth He always spoke the truth, whether it was popular or not.','know the truth At last I knew the truth about my father’s death.','find out/discover/uncover the truth She was determined to find out the truth.','learn the truth When she learns the truth, she may decide to help us.','get at/to the truth informal (= discover the truth ) The police will eventually get to the truth of the matter.','reveal the truth She’d promised never to reveal the truth.','accept/admit the truth Our pride kept us from admitting the truth.','be/come close to the truth The book comes a little too close to the truth for their liking.','get the truth out of somebody (= make someone tell you the truth ) I’ll get the truth out of her, whatever it takes!','the whole/full truth Investors should have been told the whole truth.','the simple/plain/naked truth (= the truth, with nothing added, left out, or hidden ) The simple truth is that there isn’t enough money to pay for it.','the sad/painful truth (= something that is true but that you regret ) She still misses him, and that’s the sad truth.','the awful/terrible/dreadful etc truth She could not bring herself to tell them the awful truth.','the honest truth (= used to emphasize that you are telling the truth ) We never came here to steal anything, and that’s the honest truth.','the gospel truth (= the complete truth ) Don’t take everything she says as the gospel truth.','the truth of the matter The truth of the matter is that we don’t know what really happened.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('c182121c-c035-593a-b7bf-0076a0ec1a5e','1af0b85a-4dc9-57f2-860a-a2e4c48b66ed',2,'being true','واقعی بودن','spoken & written','the state or quality of being true','[ uncountable ]',null,'حالت یا کیفیت واقعی بودن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['tell the truth It’s better to tell the truth.','speak the truth He always spoke the truth, whether it was popular or not.','know the truth At last I knew the truth about my father’s death.','find out/discover/uncover the truth She was determined to find out the truth.','learn the truth When she learns the truth, she may decide to help us.','get at/to the truth informal (= discover the truth ) The police will eventually get to the truth of the matter.','reveal the truth She’d promised never to reveal the truth.','accept/admit the truth Our pride kept us from admitting the truth.','be/come close to the truth The book comes a little too close to the truth for their liking.','get the truth out of somebody (= make someone tell you the truth ) I’ll get the truth out of her, whatever it takes!','the whole/full truth Investors should have been told the whole truth.','the simple/plain/naked truth (= the truth, with nothing added, left out, or hidden ) The simple truth is that there isn’t enough money to pay for it.','the sad/painful truth (= something that is true but that you regret ) She still misses him, and that’s the sad truth.','the awful/terrible/dreadful etc truth She could not bring herself to tell them the awful truth.','the honest truth (= used to emphasize that you are telling the truth ) We never came here to steal anything, and that’s the honest truth.','the gospel truth (= the complete truth ) Don’t take everything she says as the gospel truth.','the truth of the matter The truth of the matter is that we don’t know what really happened.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There was some truth in the accusations.","translation":"در این اتهامات تا حدی حقیقت وجود داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000562658.mp3"},{"sentence":"There wasn’t a grain of truth in what he said.","translation":"ذره ای از حقیقت در صحبت های او وجود نداشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000562662.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was an element of truth (= a small amount of truth ) in what he said.","translation":"در سخنان او عنصری از صدق (= مقدار کمی از حقیقت) وجود داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001600171.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is no truth in the rumour.","translation":"هیچ حقیقتی در شایعه وجود ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001600170.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('16bfc155-41ba-5848-89fe-ec11abbf35b0','1af0b85a-4dc9-57f2-860a-a2e4c48b66ed',3,'important ideas','ایده های مهم','formal','an important fact or idea that is accepted as being true','[ countable usually plural ]',null,'یک واقعیت یا ایده مهم که به عنوان واقعیت پذیرفته شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['tell the truth It’s better to tell the truth.','speak the truth He always spoke the truth, whether it was popular or not.','know the truth At last I knew the truth about my father’s death.','find out/discover/uncover the truth She was determined to find out the truth.','learn the truth When she learns the truth, she may decide to help us.','get at/to the truth informal (= discover the truth ) The police will eventually get to the truth of the matter.','reveal the truth She’d promised never to reveal the truth.','accept/admit the truth Our pride kept us from admitting the truth.','be/come close to the truth The book comes a little too close to the truth for their liking.','get the truth out of somebody (= make someone tell you the truth ) I’ll get the truth out of her, whatever it takes!','the whole/full truth Investors should have been told the whole truth.','the simple/plain/naked truth (= the truth, with nothing added, left out, or hidden ) The simple truth is that there isn’t enough money to pay for it.','the sad/painful truth (= something that is true but that you regret ) She still misses him, and that’s the sad truth.','the awful/terrible/dreadful etc truth She could not bring herself to tell them the awful truth.','the honest truth (= used to emphasize that you are telling the truth ) We never came here to steal anything, and that’s the honest truth.','the gospel truth (= the complete truth ) Don’t take everything she says as the gospel truth.','the truth of the matter The truth of the matter is that we don’t know what really happened.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The experience has taught us some basic truths .","translation":"تجربه برخی از حقایق اساسی را به ما آموخته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001600176.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is in his interest to hide unhappy truths about his agency’s performance.","translation":"به نفع اوست که حقایق ناخوشایند درباره عملکرد آژانس خود را پنهان کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001600183.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c2bdef07-776b-51de-bf75-42f382537732','1af0b85a-4dc9-57f2-860a-a2e4c48b66ed',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'in truth','حقیقت، راستی؛ حقیقت (طی)؛ حقیقت (زندگی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['tell the truth It’s better to tell the truth.','speak the truth He always spoke the truth, whether it was popular or not.','know the truth At last I knew the truth about my father’s death.','find out/discover/uncover the truth She was determined to find out the truth.','learn the truth When she learns the truth, she may decide to help us.','get at/to the truth informal (= discover the truth ) The police will eventually get to the truth of the matter.','reveal the truth She’d promised never to reveal the truth.','accept/admit the truth Our pride kept us from admitting the truth.','be/come close to the truth The book comes a little too close to the truth for their liking.','get the truth out of somebody (= make someone tell you the truth ) I’ll get the truth out of her, whatever it takes!','the whole/full truth Investors should have been told the whole truth.','the simple/plain/naked truth (= the truth, with nothing added, left out, or hidden ) The simple truth is that there isn’t enough money to pay for it.','the sad/painful truth (= something that is true but that you regret ) She still misses him, and that’s the sad truth.','the awful/terrible/dreadful etc truth She could not bring herself to tell them the awful truth.','the honest truth (= used to emphasize that you are telling the truth ) We never came here to steal anything, and that’s the honest truth.','the gospel truth (= the complete truth ) Don’t take everything she says as the gospel truth.','the truth of the matter The truth of the matter is that we don’t know what really happened.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
