('16f4f428-93d7-5a25-b073-4418b36af6df','574d6ab2-aba2-54fc-a198-96731c444924',13,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'watch the world go by','تماشا کردن، نگاه کردن (به)؛ مواظب بودن (بر)؛ تماشا (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['watch television We watched television all evening.','watch a programme/film/show They were watching a film on TV.','closely I watched him closely while he was giving his evidence.','carefully She watched very carefully and did exactly as he did.','helplessly He watched helplessly as his son was swept away by the waves.','intently (= with a lot of attention ) Her father was watching her intently as she worked.','with interest/amusement etc A small crowd of people were watching them with interest.','in horror/amazement etc He watched in horror as the flames engulfed his house.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('20e1c782-ebf7-531b-b7bc-fb2b5fd4cc81','574d6ab2-aba2-54fc-a198-96731c444924',14,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'you watch','تماشا کردن، نگاه کردن (به)؛ مواظب بودن (بر)؛ تماشا (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['watch television We watched television all evening.','watch a programme/film/show They were watching a film on TV.','closely I watched him closely while he was giving his evidence.','carefully She watched very carefully and did exactly as he did.','helplessly He watched helplessly as his son was swept away by the waves.','intently (= with a lot of attention ) Her father was watching her intently as she worked.','with interest/amusement etc A small crowd of people were watching them with interest.','in horror/amazement etc He watched in horror as the flames engulfed his house.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('3d7eba76-d7c7-5a20-bf33-8e14d4779cbf','1e1917c3-699f-5c00-8310-2a1cbdc19d47',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a small clock that you wear on your wrist or keep in your pocket','[ countable ]',null,'ساعت مچی، ساعت (دستی)؛ نگهبانی (فرد)؛ ساعت (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['look at/glance at your watch I looked at my watch. It was 4.30.','check/consult your watch He checked his watch and saw that it was only 2.15.','a watch says ... My watch says twenty past one.','put your watch forward (= make it show a later time ) The passengers were reminded to put their watches forward three hours.','put your watch back (= make it show an earlier time ) On Saturday night, don’t forget to put your watch back an hour.','set your watch (= make it show the correct time ) I set my watch by the clock on the mantelpiece.','wear a watch He wore a gold watch.','a watch stops Her watch had stopped after getting wet in the sea.','somebody’s watch is fast/runs fast (= it shows a later time ) No, it’s only 12.15 – your watch must be fast.','somebody’s watch is slow/runs slow (= it shows an earlier time ) ''He’s late.'' ''Maybe his watch is running slow.''']::text[],'[{"sentence":"My watch has stopped .","translation":"ساعت من متوقف شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000509279.mp3"},{"sentence":"She glanced nervously at her watch.","translation":"نگاهی عصبی به ساعتش انداخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001602641.mp3"},{"sentence":"How do you keep track of time if you don’t wear a watch ?","translation":"اگر ساعت نزنید چگونه زمان را پیگیری می کنید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001602642.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('7bf206c7-9342-51f2-bdcf-6260acb9803e','1e1917c3-699f-5c00-8310-2a1cbdc19d47',2,null,null,'spoken & written','when you watch someone or something carefully, or pay careful attention to them, so that you are ready to act if necessary','[ singular, uncountable ]',null,'وقتی کسی یا چیزی را با دقت تماشا می کنید یا به آنها توجه می کنید تا در صورت لزوم آماده باشید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['look at/glance at your watch I looked at my watch. It was 4.30.','check/consult your watch He checked his watch and saw that it was only 2.15.','a watch says ... My watch says twenty past one.','put your watch forward (= make it show a later time ) The passengers were reminded to put their watches forward three hours.','put your watch back (= make it show an earlier time ) On Saturday night, don’t forget to put your watch back an hour.','set your watch (= make it show the correct time ) I set my watch by the clock on the mantelpiece.','wear a watch He wore a gold watch.','a watch stops Her watch had stopped after getting wet in the sea.','somebody’s watch is fast/runs fast (= it shows a later time ) No, it’s only 12.15 – your watch must be fast.','somebody’s watch is slow/runs slow (= it shows an earlier time ) ''He’s late.'' ''Maybe his watch is running slow.''']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The police arrived to keep watch on the mouth of the tunnel.","translation":"پلیس برای مراقبت از دهانه تونل وارد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001602649.mp3"},{"sentence":"He maintained a 24-hour watch over his son.","translation":"او 24 ساعت مراقب پسرش بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001602648.mp3"},{"sentence":"Security forces kept a close watch on our activities.","translation":"نیروهای امنیتی به دقت فعالیت های ما را زیر نظر داشتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001978304.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ec2b0277-88fa-564e-af5a-a551014ad153','1e1917c3-699f-5c00-8310-2a1cbdc19d47',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'keep a watch out for somebody/something','ساعت مچی، ساعت (دستی)؛ نگهبانی (فرد)؛ ساعت (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['look at/glance at your watch I looked at my watch. It was 4.30.','check/consult your watch He checked his watch and saw that it was only 2.15.','a watch says ... My watch says twenty past one.','put your watch forward (= make it show a later time ) The passengers were reminded to put their watches forward three hours.','put your watch back (= make it show an earlier time ) On Saturday night, don’t forget to put your watch back an hour.','set your watch (= make it show the correct time ) I set my watch by the clock on the mantelpiece.','wear a watch He wore a gold watch.','a watch stops Her watch had stopped after getting wet in the sea.','somebody’s watch is fast/runs fast (= it shows a later time ) No, it’s only 12.15 – your watch must be fast.','somebody’s watch is slow/runs slow (= it shows an earlier time ) ''He’s late.'' ''Maybe his watch is running slow.''']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('06ad619f-b502-5ae9-8b25-d2ce1e9f460b','1e1917c3-699f-5c00-8310-2a1cbdc19d47',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a group of people whose job is to guard or protect someone or something','[ countable ]','neighbourhood watch','گروهی از مردم که وظیفه آنها محافظت یا محافظت از کسی یا چیزی است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['look at/glance at your watch I looked at my watch. It was 4.30.','check/consult your watch He checked his watch and saw that it was only 2.15.','a watch says ... My watch says twenty past one.','put your watch forward (= make it show a later time ) The passengers were reminded to put their watches forward three hours.','put your watch back (= make it show an earlier time ) On Saturday night, don’t forget to put your watch back an hour.','set your watch (= make it show the correct time ) I set my watch by the clock on the mantelpiece.','wear a watch He wore a gold watch.','a watch stops Her watch had stopped after getting wet in the sea.','somebody’s watch is fast/runs fast (= it shows a later time ) No, it’s only 12.15 – your watch must be fast.','somebody’s watch is slow/runs slow (= it shows an earlier time ) ''He’s late.'' ''Maybe his watch is running slow.''']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We were arrested and held until the arrival of the night watch (= people responsible for keeping the streets safe at night, especially in past times ) .","translation":"ما را دستگیر کردند و تا رسیدن نگهبان شب (= افرادی که مسئول حفظ امنیت خیابان ها در شب، به ویژه در زمان های گذشته بودند) بازداشت شدیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001602667.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('768a172d-38f5-5d65-955d-850b9576de87','1e1917c3-699f-5c00-8310-2a1cbdc19d47',5,null,null,'spoken & written','a period of time when it is someone’s duty to stay somewhere and look for signs of danger','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'یک دوره زمانی که وظیفه کسی است که در جایی بماند و به دنبال علائم خطر باشد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['look at/glance at your watch I looked at my watch. It was 4.30.','check/consult your watch He checked his watch and saw that it was only 2.15.','a watch says ... My watch says twenty past one.','put your watch forward (= make it show a later time ) The passengers were reminded to put their watches forward three hours.','put your watch back (= make it show an earlier time ) On Saturday night, don’t forget to put your watch back an hour.','set your watch (= make it show the correct time ) I set my watch by the clock on the mantelpiece.','wear a watch He wore a gold watch.','a watch stops Her watch had stopped after getting wet in the sea.','somebody’s watch is fast/runs fast (= it shows a later time ) No, it’s only 12.15 – your watch must be fast.','somebody’s watch is slow/runs slow (= it shows an earlier time ) ''He’s late.'' ''Maybe his watch is running slow.''']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The first watch is from now until midnight.","translation":"اولین ساعت از الان تا نیمه شب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000509317.mp3"},{"sentence":"Who’s on watch tonight?","translation":"چه کسی امشب مراقب است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000509320.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('cd28a967-e26a-5228-b85b-9779e0de89b1','5fa15e17-70c3-5eb6-8100-152bb91c72d0',1,'liquid','مایع','spoken & written','the clear liquid without colour , smell , or taste that falls as rain and that is used for drinking , washing etc',null,null,'آب، آب (خوراکی)؛ آب (سالی)؛ آب (تلفن)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['drinking water (= water that you can drink safely ) There is no source of drinking water on the island.','tap water (= water that comes out of a tap ) The tap water is not safe to drink.','bottled water (= water to drink that you buy in bottles ) Sales of bottled water have rocketed.','mineral water (= water that has natural substances in it, and is sold in bottles ) The mineral water comes from the Scottish mountain.','spring water (= water that comes naturally out of the ground and has not been treated with any chemicals, usually sold in bottles ) I ordered a glass of spring water.','running water (= water that comes out of a system of pipes into buildings ) Only half the city’s houses had running water.','fresh water (= water in lakes, rivers etc that does not contain salt ) This bird is usually found in open country near fresh water.','salt water (= water from the sea, or water to which salt has been added ) He washed his hands in a pool of salt water.','hard (= containing a lot of calcium ) Hard water is formed as rainwater passes down through layers of limestone.','soft (= not containing much calcium ) In our area the water is quite soft.','hot There isn''t any hot water!','cold The water in the pool was pretty cold.','lukewarm (= only slightly warm ) Stir the yeast into lukewarm water.','clean Millions of people do not have access to clean drinking water.','dirty Diseases can be spread by dirty water.','contaminated (= water that has harmful substances in it ) They became ill from drinking contaminated water.','soapy Wash your hands with hot soapy water.','the water supply (= water and the lakes, reservoirs etc where it is stored ) A dam was built to improve the water supply.','a water shortage There is a severe water shortage in many parts of the country.','a glass of water She poured herself a glass of water.','a drink of water He asked for a drink of water.','turn the water off/on (= turn a tap to stop water coming out of pipes or to let it come out ) Turn the water off while you''re brushing your teeth.','water runs I let the cool water run down my back.','water flows We watched the water flow under the bridge.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There’s water all over the bathroom floor.","translation":"تمام کف حمام آب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942814.mp3"},{"sentence":"Does anyone want a drink of water ?","translation":"آیا کسی آب می‌خواهد؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942815.mp3"},{"sentence":"a glass of sparkling mineral water","translation":"یک لیوان آب معدنی گازدار","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942819.mp3"},{"sentence":"All rooms have hot and cold running water .","translation":"همه اتاق ها دارای آب سرد و گرم هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942822.mp3"},{"sentence":"Pour boiling water over the rice and let it soak.","translation":"روی برنج آب جوش بریزید و بگذارید خیس بخورد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942826.mp3"},{"sentence":"a fresh water spring","translation":"چشمه آب شیرین","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942830.mp3"},{"sentence":"When dealing with a burst pipe, always turn off the water first.","translation":"هنگام برخورد با ترکیدگی لوله، همیشه ابتدا آب را ببندید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942834.mp3"},{"sentence":"contamination of the local water supply","translation":"آلودگی منبع آب محلی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001942838.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
('e682e796-b9a2-53fe-b1a3-250a5073c042','5fa15e17-70c3-5eb6-8100-152bb91c72d0',2,'area of water','منطقه آب','spoken & written','an area of water such as the sea , a lake etc',null,null,'منطقه ای از آب مانند دریا، دریاچه و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['drinking water (= water that you can drink safely ) There is no source of drinking water on the island.','tap water (= water that comes out of a tap ) The tap water is not safe to drink.','bottled water (= water to drink that you buy in bottles ) Sales of bottled water have rocketed.','mineral water (= water that has natural substances in it, and is sold in bottles ) The mineral water comes from the Scottish mountain.','spring water (= water that comes naturally out of the ground and has not been treated with any chemicals, usually sold in bottles ) I ordered a glass of spring water.','running water (= water that comes out of a system of pipes into buildings ) Only half the city’s houses had running water.','fresh water (= water in lakes, rivers etc that does not contain salt ) This bird is usually found in open country near fresh water.','salt water (= water from the sea, or water to which salt has been added ) He washed his hands in a pool of salt water.','hard (= containing a lot of calcium ) Hard water is formed as rainwater passes down through layers of limestone.','soft (= not containing much calcium ) In our area the water is quite soft.','hot There isn''t any hot water!','cold The water in the pool was pretty cold.','lukewarm (= only slightly warm ) Stir the yeast into lukewarm water.','clean Millions of people do not have access to clean drinking water.','dirty Diseases can be spread by dirty water.','contaminated (= water that has harmful substances in it ) They became ill from drinking contaminated water.','soapy Wash your hands with hot soapy water.','the water supply (= water and the lakes, reservoirs etc where it is stored ) A dam was built to improve the water supply.','a water shortage There is a severe water shortage in many parts of the country.','a glass of water She poured herself a glass of water.','a drink of water He asked for a drink of water.','turn the water off/on (= turn a tap to stop water coming out of pipes or to let it come out ) Turn the water off while you''re brushing your teeth.','water runs I let the cool water run down my back.','water flows We watched the water flow under the bridge.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Rangoon is surrounded on three sides by water.","translation":"رانگون از سه طرف توسط آب احاطه شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001602747.mp3"},{"sentence":"Denzil dived into the water.","translation":"دنزیل در آب شیرجه زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001602753.mp3"},{"sentence":"He stepped down to the water’s edge.","translation":"تا لبه آب پایین آمد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000509512.mp3"},{"sentence":"The temple can only be reached by water.","translation":"دسترسی به معبد فقط از طریق آب امکان پذیر است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000509517.mp3"},{"sentence":"something floating on the water","translation":"چیزی روی آب شناور است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000509522.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
